    "title": "Tests fail when run inside ralph loop due to environment contamination: (1) ralph.test.ts KSPEC_RALP",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "**What**: Three tests fail when run inside a ralph loop because they inherit environment variables from the parent ralph process instead of running in a clean env:\n\n1. `tests/ralph.test.ts` line ~618: The test asserts `KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION` is null for non-ralph child processes, but when tests run inside a ralph loop, the env var leaks from the parent process via `...process.env` spread (line 40).\n\n2. `tests/session-create.test.ts`: The `kspecJson()` helper parses stdout as JSON, but when KSPEC_SESSION_ID is inherited from ralph, the session-create command emits an \"active session\" warning to stderr that contaminates the output parsing.\n\n3. `tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts`: References a nonexistent `task set-automation` command (the actual command is `task set --automation`).\n\n**Where**:\n- `tests/ralph.test.ts` — `runRalph()` helper (lines 27-56), env propagation test (lines 591-619)\n- `tests/session-create.test.ts` — tests using `kspecJson()` for session creation\n- `tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts` — the test referencing `set-automation`\n- `tests/helpers/cli.ts` — the `kspec()` and `kspecJson()` helpers\n\n**How**:\n- In `runRalph()` and test helpers that spawn child processes, explicitly delete `KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION` and `KSPEC_SESSION_ID` from the env spread unless the test specifically tests those vars. The pattern at line 601-603 already shows the approach.\n- Apply the same cleanup to the `kspec()` and `kspecJson()` helpers in `tests/helpers/cli.ts` so ALL test invocations are isolated from parent ralph env vars by default.\n- Fix the `set-automation` reference to use the correct `task set --automation` command syntax.\n\n**Done when**:\n- All three test files pass both standalone (`npm test`) and when run inside a ralph loop\n- The `kspec()` / `kspecJson()` test helpers strip `KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION` and `KSPEC_SESSION_ID` from inherited env by default\n- Tests that need these vars explicitly pass them via the `env` option",
